\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Real actions and Gaussian states}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Real fields first acquire a topology, measurable events and a
reference volume. The following prerequisites specify those structures
before a [positive quadratic action](fdip-0004) is chosen. Its normalized
Gaussian law turns integrable observables into expectations and supplies a
[state on polynomial functions](fdip-002A), with
[inverse precision as covariance](fdip-000B). The [massless case](fdip-000C)
shows why constant modes and the chosen constraint cannot be ignored;
these probability statements use real measure and positivity.}

